Package: violoop-edge-kiosk-qt
Version: VERSION_PLACEHOLDER
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: ARCH_PLACEHOLDER
Maintainer: doctor <doctor@bvio.ai>
Depends: violoop-qt6 (>= 6.8.5-violoop4), weston, fonts-noto-cjk, fonts-noto-core, fonts-dejavu-core, fonts-noto-color-emoji, libstdc++6
Replaces: violoop-edge-front
Homepage: https://github.com/BvioTech/violoop-edge-front3
Description: Violoop Edge device kiosk UI (Qt/QML, evaluation build)
 Qt/QML reimplementation of the device kiosk front-end, evaluating
 replacing the production Flutter app (violoop-edge-front /
 violoop-edge-kiosk.service, see sibling violoop-edge-front2). Declares
 Replaces against violoop-edge-front in preparation for that cutover -
 we're still pre-production, so this is groundwork, not an active
 takeover (no Conflicts/Breaks against that package yet, so both can
 still be installed side by side). This package's own
 violoop-edge-kiosk-qt.service IS enabled and started automatically on
 install (see postinst): it conflicts at the systemd level with the
 production violoop-edge-kiosk.service, so starting it stops that one.
 .
 Links against /opt/violoop-qt6 (package violoop-qt6), BvioTech's own
 Qt 6.8.5 build with the GLES/ESSL100 and qtquicktimeline fixes this
 repo's qt3d-spike found necessary on this device - not the Debian
 system qt6-* packages, which reproduce that bug.
